data: {"type": "final", "payload": "## 核查结论\n\n**该论断证据不足，无法成立。** 文献库中没有任何研究能直接支持\"大语言模型的使用**必然**显著增加**所有学科**的学术不端行为\"这一绝对化结论。现有证据只能说明 LLM 对学术诚信**构成挑战**，但远不足以支撑\"必然\"\"所有学科\"\"显著增加\"这三个限定词。\n\n### 一、相关讨论（有文献，但只是讨论而非直接证据）\n\n文献库中有大量论文讨论 LLM 与学术诚信的关系，但多为**观点性、综述性或单点实证**，而非对\"必然增加所有学科不端\"的因果证明：\n\n- 《ChatGPT: The End of Online Exam Integrity?》(2022) 评估了 ChatGPT 生成与人类难以区分文本的能力，讨论其对考试诚信的威胁——这是**能力层面的讨论**，未证明实际不端行为必然增加。\n- 《Academic Integrity considerations of AI Large Language Models in the post-pandemic era》(2023) 综述了 LLM 对学术诚信的考量，覆盖数学、心理学、工程伦理、政治学等多学科——属于**风险讨论**。\n- 《Survey on AI-Generated Plagiarism Detection》(2024) 引用了 2023 年对 3,017 名学生的调查，约三分之一承认使用 ChatGPT 辅助——这是**单一调查的自我报告数据**，且\"使用辅助\"不等于\"学术不端\"，更不等于\"所有学科显著增加\"。\n\n### 二、直接证据（缺失）\n\n- verify_claim 判定该论断为**\"证据不足\"**，最高接地相似度 0.84 的文献立场为**中立（NEUTRAL）**，即相关文献只是提及 LLM 与学术诚信的关联，并未给出支持\"必然显著增加所有学科\"的因果证据。\n- 检索到的实证研究（如学生感知调查、单学科案例）均为**局部、情境化**证据，无法外推到\"所有学科\"。\n- 文献中反而存在**反方向**的讨论：如《The impact of large language models on higher education》(2024) 强调 LLM 可促进自主学习、需人类监督，说明其影响并非单向负面。\n\n### 三、结论\n\n\"必然\"\"所有学科\"\"显著增加\"这三个词把一项**存在争议、情境依赖的风险**夸大成了一条**普适的因果定律**。现有文献只能支持\"LLM 对学术诚信构成真实且广泛的挑战\"这一较弱表述，无法支持该绝对论断。若需更精确的结论，需要针对具体学科、具体使用场景的实证研究，而非笼统断言。", "meta": {"runtime": "langgraph", "node": "reflect", "phase": "自检修正", "elapsed_ms": 939, "session_id": "a04b-insufficient-20260810", "stop_reason": "completed", "tokens_in": 8918, "tokens_out": 576, "structured_answer": {"schema_version": "answer-contract/v1", "capability": "claim_verification", "status": "evidence_insufficient", "verdict_label": "证据不足", "answer_mode": "evidence_based", "citation_compliance": "not_applicable", "citations": [{"paper_id": "41503652", "title": "Innovative Application of Large Language Models in Biology and Medicine Under Artificial Intelligence for Science Paradigm.", "year": 2025, "chunk_uid": "a3f664d37e96da3e02577fb9c18e43ca8fd1924a", "source_field": "abstract", "evidence_sentence": "Currently,the artificial intelligence for science paradigm is evolving rapidly,with the new generation of artificial intelligence technologies represented by large language models(LLM)having injected transformative momentum into biological and medical research.", "stance": "NEUTRAL", "confidence": 0.5}, {"paper_id": "W4387576300", "title": "ChatGPT is not capable of serving as an author: ethical concerns and challenges of large language models in education", "year": 2023, "chunk_uid": "5934ae144d4c9c8b994ce9b876a758f47ab8349c", "source_field": "abstract", "evidence_sentence": "It sheds light on their set of limitations, ethical concerns, and challenges that must be addressed thoughtfully, offering a comprehensive exploration of the", "stance": "NEUTRAL", "confidence": 0.5}, {"paper_id": "W4407057275", "title": "The use of large language models as scaffolds for proleptic reasoning", "year": 2025, "chunk_uid": "1bc3549bac725762d09193e7a8ce71970bb45c06", "source_field": "abstract", "evidence_sentence": "Although LLM outputs often evoke fascination and resemble human writing, they are unpredictable and must be used with discernment.", "stance": "NEUTRAL", "confidence": 0.5}, {"paper_id": "W4409241400", "title": "Integrating Large Language Models into the Chemistry and Materials Science Laboratory Curricula", "year": 2025, "chunk_uid": "30d65af4a363f39b34013b91f9686839651a0754", "source_field": "abstract", "evidence_sentence": "With the recent rise of large language models (LLMs) such as ChatGPT and Gemini, these once-fantastical visions", "stance": "NEUTRAL", "confidence": 0.5}], "uncertainty": {"category": "evidence_insufficient", "message": "未检索到明确支持或反驳的证据。", "calibrated_rejection": true, "qualification_hints": ["证据仅提及LLM对科研的推动作用，未涉及学术不端行为。", "证据提及伦理关切，但未明确指向学术不端行为的必然增加。", "证据强调需谨慎使用，但未断言必然增加学术不端。", "证据仅描述LLM在教育中的应用愿景，未涉及学术不端。", "证据提及LLM的幻觉问题，但未与学术不端行为直接关联。", "证据讨论临床试验挑战，未涉及学术不端行为。"]}, "tool_basis": ["verify_claim"], "claim": "大语言模型的使用必然会显著增加所有学科的学术不端行为"}}}

